    {
        "content": "<p>The <code>ext</code> tactic on matrices produces goals which are not type-correct at implicit, which is breaking my later <code>simp</code> calls.</p>\n<p>Here's my MWE:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">LinearAlgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Defs</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tacticCheckInstances</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">warning: declaration uses `sorry`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">---</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">warning: produced tactic goal is not type-correct at `.implicit` transparency; consider using propositional rewriting or marking some of the following as `@[implicit_reducible]`:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  Matrix</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">Full error:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  function expected</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    A i</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">Note: This linter can be disabled with `set_option linter.tacticCheckInstances false`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 623308640,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1789090382
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I looked into Matrix once, and it seems that the wide use of <code>M i j</code> where <code>M</code> is a matrix but used as a function is largely considered bad by Lean, and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.ext#doc\">docs#Matrix.ext</a> is one of them</p>",
        "id": 623310101,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1789091108
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One way to fix this is to change every such instance to the type-correct <code>Matrix.of.symm M i j</code></p>",
        "id": 623310225,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1789091172
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another way would be to mark <code>Matrix</code> as <code>implicit_reducible</code>, which (IIUC) wouldn't impact instances but is what has happened to other type synonyms.</p>",
        "id": 623311580,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1789091888
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Adding a <code>FunLike</code> instance <a href=\"https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=JYWwDg9gTgLgBAWQIYwBYBtgCMB0ARFJHAMQFcA7AGWAGsBTHAISQGdgBjAKE5bpgH0IYGMAjk4mcjDpQcMJOxHsAwqjrsaASXIt55dnRZwYUUnW4ABANqgwmdsAFQ6AE1IOs6OgF1OLugBmiChQwAAecAAUIHAAXHAAKgCeYHQAVACUUeLxyamZUYCNwHGJKelZuWVw%2FHEAvJxwcDGASYRw4q2F3ORIIIZgCnTBJuGcAG5IoUiegwDeMeKFAL5wMwhwAHIlyMMR83BL3MA6egYlZFS0g5Hbobtt%2B1kxke0PcADuas4NcOwQg2uxWqIb6%2FOj8I4AK3UIlGg0BcHOilE5BwkOhwFh4Jc3DQdGgdBidDCAmAASC8UigAAiODAOAQgA0cEAi4RrWkQuBApmbNlZQAphIgORs6t9ABfkAQocFQcEAZYRwcXkInweU0mVyiiKuAAHgAPpKaYzlVLZVgknA2OA4FZUN5AJfklisit8SEwrDgIsVjP4NrqcEV4LJ3CJPTsVwAgnBGFsQuEosQjnAAIxZSJx8RJjYoCpwcNAyPwk3fDVs74saBQJKcIA\">works</a>, but <code>M i j</code> doesn't use it unless we put a coercion arrow.<br>\nMaybe an app elaborator could solve this (although it depends on the type of the head rather than its name), or a nice notation <code>M[i, j]</code> defined as <code>⇑M i j</code> or <code>M.row i j</code> (<a href=\"https://live.lean-lang.org/#%2BOYArdREGmtu4ZcVRcg4N4fYBfF4WbgsS4BCyFCDyERiDwARgADKjEHAAEQAbSxcGA2IANNi4K9sQBdfEZAB8cEAi4RDQmvbhCOjiSh0JDiAAKZxgMF8fLm0igcDwdHQrWgKGgcAAyqQsABRRxgMVzTgAARxSDAYH4VilWHFy2o9BwTwpnAq8jgVlsRtaGycw3hKAB8QlxsyDxO7LdMB5PIA8sJPQBzPjB1VgTDsYDwAA8AB8%2FWpyMGw4jxFGgzzAx6xHBU37E6gQ18oABBfVwADs9ogD3a8DoarFgATCOB52NQFt8XI0WtgRvpcdpSdMsmZODt9VwFNwaxIYDoUhnAfwIbdp0mhBbglwXeS1oEw%2Fkk8%2Blk5I7lkfVqARpsPHIAAxcABIEDjP8ASZ%2BrwUsE3BoHQ0B0O47YCMA1i2F4LiAABER6vCSP7%2FmSFJwHcww4hhQGhIAKYSYjhvo5IAF%2BTWBQcCoHAgBlhMuFDQYx4iEgxVHkMxqY0QSJIcTxDFYL4cBsOAcA4qgFKAJfk3A6tB1pIJgrBwOR0EkvwUmztBLxwdwAD0AC0BnHM05BzBGXhWOwUpQEW4ikLwRhviw0BQL4b5wAZemcAAxBGpDNBY%2FAgCwEZGJq7blHGazVnAjBjPYTiuMQcxwMioQuCl4jpSMKDJHAsV3PFPxCQ8zHMg8LlQG5nBAA\">code</a>).</p>",
